Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 03:53:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 14/19] feat(embed): the review panel in the editor's reviewer
 layout

The panel host apps embed now looks and works like the editor's reviewer
layout (feat(ui), the dock): the frame takes the window, one dock floats
along the bottom and the comments float at the right, so someone who
reviews in doop and in a host app meets one tool.

- The dock: the frame's name and its status, the Hand (drag to move) and
  Comment (click the frame to pin one), the zoom (out, fit, in), Compare,
  the comments toggle with its count, then Request changes and Approve,
  which keep their words beside the icon: they are the decision.
- The comments panel has the verdict History as its second tab, starts
  open when the frame has open comments and closed otherwise, and ends
  above the dock. Request changes opens it on the composer with Comment
  picked, so the next click pins the comment.
- No header and no footer; messages show above the dock. When the host
  app picks no frame, the frames list floats at the left.
- Its own few icons and its own small helper, so the panel bundle stays
  the same size (embed JS 20 KB, CSS 7 KB, plus the shared React and
  frame runtime chunk).

Checked end to end with the stand-in host app (perf/embed-e2e.mjs in the
build repo): request changes with a pinned comment, the revision,
compare, approve, a reviewer edit refused; same results as before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
